Inventory Optimization to predict sales forecasting/stock outs/re-order point/replinishment
    The task is to fine tune the model to achieve the best possible outcome to keep the inventory lean and manage the sales during the seasonal & non-seasonal demands efficiently and meet customer expectations on time.
Tech Stack
🚀 Platform & Tools
	•	Google Colab: Cloud-based notebook environment for running code and experiments.
	•	Google Gemini: Advanced AI model from Google for machine learning tasks and experimentation.
💻 Programming Language
	•	Python: Widely used for machine learning, data analysis, and prototyping.
🛠 Core Libraries
	•	TensorFlow: Open-source platform for machine learning, deep learning, and neural network training.
📈 Time Series Libraries
	•	Pandas: Data manipulation and analysis, including time series handling.
	•	NumPy: Array computing and numerical operations.
	•	scikit-learn: Machine learning library with basic time series utilities.
	•	Statsmodels: Statistical analysis, forecasting, and time series modeling (e.g., ARIMA, SARIMAX).
	•	sktime: Specialized library for time series analysis and machine learning.
	•	tslearn: Machine learning tools for time series data.
	•	prophet: Open-source forecasting (by Meta), designed for time series prediction.
	•	GluonTS: Deep learning-based probabilistic time series modeling.
	•	pmdarima: Auto ARIMA modeling for time series.
	•	TensorFlow Timeseries: TensorFlow API for time series data and forecasting.
🧑💻 Models & Algorithms
	•	LSTM (Long Short-Term Memory): Recurrent neural network for sequence prediction and time series forecasting.
	•	Random Forest: Ensemble method using multiple decision trees for robust regression and classification.
	•	XGBoost: Gradient boosting framework for scalable, powerful regression and classification.
	•	Linear Regression: Simple regression model for trend analysis.
	•	Decision Tree: Tree-based regression/classification algorithm.
	•	Support Vector Regression (SVR): Powerful regression using support vector machines.
	•	K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN): Non-parametric regression and classification method.
	•	LightGBM: Fast, efficient gradient boosting algorithm for large datasets.

